Ladybird reuses the used user-select value when selected text inherits
from a parent the serializer has already visited. Blink checks
IsSelectable on the layout object in its text iterator. WebKit passes
IgnoresUserSelectNone to plainText in DOMSelection::toString unless a
site quirk asks for the excluded text. Gecko passes SkipInvisibleContent
to its document encoder in Selection::Stringify.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0 and WebKit 26.5 all kept the
selected SVG text and the tab between selected table cells. Ladybird
matched Chrome and Firefox for nested user-select overrides and for
slotted text. WebKit included text from the excluded ancestor in both
cases. All nine selections produced the same strings on Ladybird master
and with the parent value reused.
